{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"First, we note that $r=7$ makes the denominator zero and so cannot be a solution.\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the equation by $r-7$ to get rid of the quotient. ","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{4r - 6}{r - 7} \u0026= \\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n(r-7)\\cdot \\dfrac{4r - 6}{r - 7} \u0026= (r-7)\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n4r-6\u0026=\\dfrac12 r-\\dfrac72\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac72 r\u0026=\\dfrac52\n\\\\\\\\\nr\u0026=\\dfrac57\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We get that $r=\\dfrac57$ is a potential solution. It doesn't make the denominator zero, so it is indeed a solution.\n\n**In conclusion, $r = \\dfrac{5}{7}$.**","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Solve for $r$.**\n\n$\\dfrac{4r - 6}{r - 7} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$\n\n$r =$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":0,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":0.7142857142857143}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"","multipleNumberInput":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
